{{Quote|This is Kalevala. It's another planet in the Mandalorian system.|[[Din Djarin]]|<ref name="Apostate" />}}
'''Kalevala''' was a [[planet]] located in the [[Mandalore system]], within the [[Mandalore sector]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]]. It was the [[homeworld]] of [[House Kryze]], the prominent Mandalorian political family who ruled as [[Duke]]s and Duchesses of Kalevala. As such, it was the [[Reproduction|birthplace]] of Duchess [[Satine Kryze]], leader of the [[New Mandalorians]], and the seat of power for her sister, [[Bo-Katan Kryze]], after the [[Great Purge of Mandalore|Great Purge]].

==Description==
{{Quote|Don't worry, I grew up flying these cliffs. Of course, it's been a while.|Bo-Katan Kryze, to [[R5-D4]]|<ref name="Chapter 19">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 19: The Convert}}</ref>}}
Kalevala was a terrestrial [[planet]] in the [[Mandalore system]],<ref name="Kalevala" /> a [[star system]] it shared with [[Mandalore]], the [[homeworld]] of the [[Mandalorian]]s and center of [[Mandalore sector|Mandalorian Space]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /><ref name="Beginner Game" /> It was positioned at the coordinates O-7 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]],<ref name="Beginner Game" /> relatively near the [[Hydian Way]] [[Hyperspace route|trade route]].<ref name="BMF 32" /> The rainy world was covered by grass-swept hills and plains, broken up by rock formations and the planet's various oceans.<ref name="Apostate" /><ref name="BMF 76">{{BuildFalconCite|76|Starship Fact File}}</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|Sadly, Deputy Minister Jerec perished this morning in a Death Watch bombing on Kalevala.|[[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]]|<ref name="Duchess of Mandalore" />}}
Long before the [[Clone Wars]], ancient Kalevalan ocean cruisers were used to traverse the various oceans on the planet.<ref name="BMF 76" /> This history was reflected in the work of [[Kalevala Spaceworks]], which built the ''[[Coronet]]'', a custom made [[Nau'ur-class yacht|''Nau'ur''-class yacht]] with an upper section designed to closely resemble these ancient ships.<ref name="Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref><ref name="BMF 76" />

[[File:New_Mandalorians.png|thumb|left|250px|Kalevalan natives Duchess [[Satine Kryze]] and Prince [[Tal Merrik]] occupied high posts in the [[New Mandalorians|New Mandalorian]] government]]
[[House Kryze]] was based on Kalevala,<ref name="The Star Wars Book" /> and it was was later the [[homeworld]] of [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]], leader of the [[New Mandalorians]]. Kalevala was also the homeworld of [[Prince]] [[Tal Merrik]],<ref name="Tal Merrik" /> who represented Kalevala<ref name="Kalevala" /> in the [[Galactic Senate|Senate]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]<ref name="Voyage of Temptation" /> by the [[Standard year|year]] [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> up until his [[death]] that same year.<ref name="Voyage of Temptation" /> Shortly afterwards, the [[Death Watch]], a traditionalist splinter group that opposed the New Mandalorians, was responsible for a [[Bombing on Kalevala|bombing]] on Kalevala that killed [[Deputy Minister]] [[Jerec]]. [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] used this bombing as justification for a proposed Republic [[Mandalore Defense Resolution|intervention]] on [[Mandalore]], though Duchess Satine argued against the proposal on the floor of the Galactic Senate.<ref name="Duchess of Mandalore" />

Though Mandalore itself was [[Great Purge of Mandalore|laid waste]] by the [[Galactic Empire]] in the [[Night of a Thousand Tears]], other parts of Mandalorian space like [[Concordia]] and Kalevala apparently escaped the destruction.<ref name="BOBFChapter5">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref><ref name="Apostate" /> During the [[New Republic Era]], [[Lady]] [[Bo-Katan Kryze]] retired to [[Kryze Fortress|Kryze Castle]] on Kalevala after abandoning her efforts to reclaim the Mandalorian homeworld.<ref name="Apostate" />

[[File:Kalevala.png|thumb|right|250px|Kryze Castle located on Kalevala.]]
Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|17}}</ref> the Mandalorian [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]], along with the [[Foundling]] [[Din Grogu|Grogu]], visited Kryze on Kalevala to find out the location of the [[Mines of Mandalore]]; there, Djarin hoped to redeem himself in the eyes of the [[Children of the Watch]], a cult of Mandalorian zealots, by bathing in the [[Living Waters|living waters of Mandalore]].<ref name="Apostate" /> On their [[Mission to the Living Waters|return from the living waters]], Bo-Katan and Din Djarin found Kryze Castle [[Bombing of Kryze Castle|under attack]] by [[TIE/IN interceptor|TIE Interceptors]] and [[TIE/sa tactical bomber|TIE Bombers]].<ref name="Chapter 19" /> The attack had been ordered by [[Moff]] [[Gideon]], whose [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] was secretly [[Mandalore Imperial base|headquartered]] on Mandalore.<ref name="Chapter 23">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 23: The Spies}}</ref> Together, Bo-Katan and Din Djarin were able to fend off the attack, though Kryze Castle was destroyed.<ref name="Chapter 19" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Obi-Wan Kenobi was reunited with an old friend: the Duchess Satine of Kalevala.|News reel narrator|<ref name="Voyage of Temptation" />}}
[[File:Kalevala-RyanChurch.jpg|thumb|left|270px|Concept illustration of Kryze Castle on Kalevala by [[Ryan Church]]]]
Kalevala was first mentioned in the opening news reel of "[[Voyage of Temptation]]," the thirteenth episode of the [[canon]] animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''{{'}} [[The Clone Wars: Season Two|second season]],<ref name="Voyage of Temptation" /> which originally aired on [[February 5]], [[2010]].<ref name="Voyage of Temptation air date">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/voyage-of-temptation-episode-guide|text="Voyage of Temptation" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> The planet was originally introduced in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity in ''[[The Complete Star Wars Encyclopedia]]'', a three-volume [[2008]] reference book edited by [[Bob Vitas]].<ref name="CSWE">{{CSWECite|II|195|Kalevala}}</ref> The world first appeared onscreen in "[[Chapter 17: The Apostate]]," the [[The Mandalorian Season Three|season three]] premiere of ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', filmed at [[Wikipedia:Neist Point|Neist Point]] on the [[Wikipedia:Isle of Skye|Isle of Skye]] in [[Wikipedia:Scotland|Scotland]].<ref name="Apostate" /><ref name="Neist Point Lighthoose">{{WebCite|url=https://www.photoawards.com/winner/zoom.php?eid=8-214136-21|text=Neist Point Lighthouse|author=David Nomdedeu|work=International Photography Awards|archivedate=20240524074953}}</ref>

There are two known pronunciations of Kalevala. In "Voyage of Temptation," the world's name was pronounced "Kall-vah-lah,"<ref name="Voyage of Temptation" /> while in the subsequent episode, "[[Duchess of Mandalore]]," it was instead pronounced "Kah-lay-vah-lah."<ref name="Duchess of Mandalore" /> In "The Apostate," Din Djarin uses the latter pronunciation.<ref name="Apostate" /> In ''[[The Star Wars Book]]'', Kalevala is misspelled as "Kalavela."<ref name="The Star Wars Book" />

